{"id": "EUVD-2026-64415", "enisaUuid": "0551a1e2-15ea-3179-b368-c3589ebfdf1f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: handle NULL b_addr in xfs_buf_free\n\nWhen xfs_buf_alloc_backing_mem() fails, xfs_buf_free() is called with\nbp->b_addr still NULL.  The code falls through to the folio_put path\nwhich calls virt_to_folio(NULL), dereferencing an invalid address and\ncausing a kernel crash.\n\n Call Trace:\n  xfs_buf_free+0x25f/0x510\n  xfs_buf_alloc+0xc98/0x19b0\n  xfs_buf_find_insert+0x55/0x14d0\n  xfs_buf_get_map+0x122b/0x17c0\n  xfbtree_init_leaf_block+0x11c/0x4a0\n  xfbtree_init+0x1bb/0x460\n  xrep_rmap_setup_scan+0x100/0x1f0\n  xrep_rmapbt+0x41/0xc0\n\nFix this by skipping folio_put() when bp->b_addr is NULL.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:33:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/444ff50ece93060131ad84fbd3f378723d8ac243", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ccf6738adcafa5ddbddc4e71b45d8a51b86643c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3aa0c1d23ee1b9d9b340fb2f4736536e1408d706", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d852729c5f4f830fbe7413df032e29459b3daf83"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74728", "GHSA-rrpq-4xmf-c84j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "23791c13-b486-3223-abf6-c6bab8d35360", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2829f9b3-edb2-39bc-8b14-8c34ed0fb96c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "4debe6e4-80c1-31e7-a838-761783d687f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "51b15f68-8765-3388-a6c6-c3bc8ba003d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5076a6040ca1613e616d84aecfaac5f932db84e0 <ccf6738adcafa5ddbddc4e71b45d8a51b86643c7"}, {"id": "7ddaf5b8-3c5a-34ee-bcdb-67690b4f66dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "8aadf4e6-27c5-33b4-a29e-d3e8a1ad6ead", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.45"}, {"id": "8e8611c1-fd1d-353e-89e3-f680308489f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5076a6040ca1613e616d84aecfaac5f932db84e0 <d852729c5f4f830fbe7413df032e29459b3daf83"}, {"id": "d65377f4-8ed7-380e-81fe-3f3e910570c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "da2ccb6d-1bdc-30ef-a7ad-ac7adb8e05a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5076a6040ca1613e616d84aecfaac5f932db84e0 <3aa0c1d23ee1b9d9b340fb2f4736536e1408d706"}, {"id": "f7b51607-375f-3061-badc-c8416fd8a5f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5076a6040ca1613e616d84aecfaac5f932db84e0 <444ff50ece93060131ad84fbd3f378723d8ac243"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c8c2628f-7d73-35f4-bbd7-fa4a3c514651", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}